## Summary

The directory contains the NuttX board support package (BSP) for the **SG2000** SoC, which is a RISC-V platform using the **T-Head C906** core (S-Mode, SV39 MMU). The file breakdown:

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Kconfig** | Empty (0 bytes) -- no SG2000-specific Kconfig options |
| **Make.defs** | Build definitions: sets `HEAD_ASRC` to `sg2000_head.S` and lists all `CHIP_CSRCS` |
| **chip.h** | Master chip header; includes memory map, PLIC headers, and defines `setintstack` assembly macros for SMP/non-SMP interrupt stack setup |
| **sg2000_head.S** | Boot entry point (`__start`); contains the Linux/UEFI-compatible image header (MZ magic), sets up initial stack, trap vector, and jumps to `sg2000_start` |
| **sg2000_start.c** | Main startup sequence: clears BSS, copies ramdisk (rom1fs), initializes per-CPU areas, disables MMU, sets trap vector, initializes MMU page tables, then calls `nx_start()`. Also provides `riscv_earlyserialinit()` and `riscv_serialinit()` via 16550 UART |
| **sg2000_irq.c** | IRQ initialization and control: `up_irqinitialize()` sets up PLIC (disables all interrupts, clears pending, sets priorities to 1, threshold to 0); `up_enable_irq()`/`up_disable_irq()` toggle soft/timer/external IRQs; `up_irq_enable()` enables global interrupts |
| **sg2000_irq_dispatch.c** | IRQ dispatch: `riscv_dispatch_irq()` decodes the vector, claims PLIC interrupt for external IRQs, calls `riscv_doirq()`, and writes back to PLIC claim register |
| **sg2000_timerisr.c** | Timer initialization: uses `riscv_mtimer_initialize()` with a 25 MHz timer frequency (`MTIMER_FREQ`) and `RISCV_IRQ_STIMER` |
| **sg2000_allocateheap.c** | Kernel heap allocation: `up_allocate_kheap()` returns heap from end of idle stack to `KSRAM_END` |
| **sg2000_pgalloc.c** | Page heap allocation: `up_allocate_pgheap()` returns `PGPOOL_START`/`PGPOOL_SIZE` from board memory map |
| **sg2000_mm_init.c** | MMU setup for SV39 with T-Head C906 extensions (shareable/bufferable/cacheable/strong-order bits at bits 60-63); configures L1/L2/L3 page tables, maps I/O (0x00000000-0x3FFFFFFF), PLIC (0x70000000-0x7FFFFFFF), kernel text, kernel data, and page pool; includes `mmu_flush_cache()` with C906-specific DCACHE.IALL and SYNC.S instructions |
| **sg2000_mm_init.h** | Header declaring `sg2000_kernel_mappings()` and `sg2000_mm_init()` |
| **sg2000_memorymap.h** | Defines `SG2000_IDLESTACK_BASE` as `_ebss` (with assembly/non-assembly variants) |
| **hardware/sg2000_memorymap.h** | Defines `SG2000_PLIC_BASE` as `0x70000000ul` |
| **hardware/sg2000_plic.h** | Defines PLIC register offsets: PRIORITY, ENABLE1/ENABLE2, THRESHOLD, and CLAIM (all relative to `SG2000_PLIC_BASE`) |

